  "notes": "The harmonically richest entry in this batch by a wide margin, and the only one where that is the headline: the research says minor and modal with jazz/soul-sample colour — m7, m9, altered dominants — and **real progressions rather than vamps**, with modal shifts between sections. So `extensions` is inverted against the rest of the axis (seventh 0.5 over triad 0.3), `borrowed.V` is doubled to 0.2 for the altered dominants, `harmonicRhythm` leads with `1_per_bar`, and the families include ii–v–i motion no other trap entry here carries. `melody.phraseBars` reaches 8 because the research says 4- and 8-bar progressions, and `structure` is `long_arc` rather than a loop because these records are through-composed — beat switches, tempo shifts, hooks withheld until late — which is also why `transitions.switchUpProb` is 0.35, more than double trap's. The live-feel percussion layers are a `percs` block plus a loosened `quantizeStrength` of 0.86. ⚠ `confidence` medium: the research is medium-high on the structural habits and only medium on tempo specifics, so the INFERRED parameter is `session.bpm` — the 100–160 span here is a envelope over two named lanes (trap half-time and club-leaning straight), not a measured centre. ⚠ The Jersey-club and house four-on-the-floor kits she also uses are named in `relatedGenres` rather than modelled: this entry's drum block is her trap mode, and a kick on every beat is a different archetype rather than a parameter. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
